Z||000000||flexableface||10-19-2000||09:25 AM||||i need to know what brand of tire should i buy. I plan to put them on tommorow. the tires im getting are 215/60/14. these are the brands i have found.<P>kelly chargers=70,000 miles 290$ out the door<P>BFGoodrich radial TA's 50,000 miles 287$ out the door<P>cooper cobra's 60,000 miles 275$ out the door<P>Dayton's 50,000 miles 289$ out the door<P>i  would like to know whick one of these tires are the quality wise.Wheni say out the door i mean the tires will be balanced and mounted. thanks for the help<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-19-2000||09:38 AM||||Goodrich TA<P>Longer milage harder the rubber less performance.  Since all the prices for those tire are the same..let you pocket be your guide.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-19-2000||11:00 AM||||BF Goodrich! I have always had BFG's on my car. Originally had regular T/A's now I'm running 225/50R15 Euro T/A's.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||10-19-2000||11:34 AM||||The Radial T/A's! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-19-2000||12:16 PM||||I also like the T/As.  I've been running them for many years.<P>I don't race but I do like to push the car on the twisty mountain roads a bit.||||reg||1
Z||000005||flexableface||10-19-2000||01:56 PM||||wow its a landslide. Looks like the raidal TA's are the top choice. I called another tire place and im getting the tires for only 267$ look like ill be putting them on tommorow. the tires i have now are in pretty rough condition so it should be a vast improvment. also my car staarts shaking at about 57 mph. im guessing the tires could be balnced. so tommorow ill find out if the blancing will help. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||10-19-2000||02:18 PM||||You might want to check into Firestone Firehawk SS20's also.  I had a set of the original Firestone Firehawk SS tires on my 86 SE and I loved them - they were even good in snow, unlike the Yokohama's on my 88 Coupe.  The SS20 is supposed to be an improvement on the SS.<P>Plus you might get a bargain right now because of the Firestone scandal...||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||10-19-2000||05:09 PM||||I have the Firestone SS20 on the rims that I bought and they seem to grip really well even thought the back one are a little light on tread. I really had good luck with all the BFGoodrich T/As that I've bought. That's usually all I buy for my cars.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Xtreme Fiero's||10-19-2000||06:41 PM||||I had Firestone SS10's on my 84 SE, they lasted forever but don't leave black marks though, I tried alot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula||10-19-2000||07:11 PM||||I heard that nokia tires are some of the best tires dollar for dollar.... I believe they are swiss or german and only import to a few places in the country, theres a nokia dealer around here if you want me to find ome prices for you, I've heard they are worth the week wait.  just giving an option to you||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobertVol||10-19-2000||10:00 PM||||I have the Firestone Firehawks Also. I like them. Good ride for cruising but have good grip on the corners. They are good in the water also. And as they said above because of the scandal you may get a good deal. Even those these tires had nothing to do with the models being recalled. <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/5879e870.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||10-20-2000||05:34 PM||||Not to add fuel to the fire, but I'd try to find some pricing on Dunlop D60 A2 JLB's.  I have been running these on my Formula for about 3 years now and are absolutely the best tires I have ever had.  They give me great dry, and wet traction!  The amount of grip in wet conditions is really what has impressed me!  I don't remember what the $$ was, but I think it was slightly more than what your looking at... about $80/tire out the door.  Otherwise, I'd go with the BFG TA's!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
